IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `itra-rates`

-- Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth), s 3, ss 16-20(1), Schedule 7 Parts I-III, ss 23(2), 23(6), 23AA -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- GENERATED by gen_income-tax-rates-act-1986-conform.py (scratchpad). Expected results were written by hand from the text.
-- Mode: default: each refusal is a #CHECK (typed, not run), because the installed l4 has no #ASSERT REFUSED and forcing
-- its TBD stand-in is an evaluation error (see NOTES.md). Generate with --refuse for #ASSERT REFUSED.

-- Scenario facts used (workbench scenarios/au/wa): chloe c045 (2024-10-20), the 2023-24 return, taxable income $27,500 (a
-- graduate salary from February plus an internship), scenario expectation tax nil after the low income tax offset; chloe c048
-- (2025-10-25), the 2024-25 return, taxable income $71,500, scenario expectation "tax_before_offsets": 12842; daniel d04a
-- (2033-11-30), Jarrah Legal Technologies Pty Ltd's first company return, "a base rate entity at twenty-five per cent". The
-- scenario gives Jarrah's turnover only as under $3 million; its assessable income, passive income and taxable income here are
-- ASSUMED. The October 2024 arrival's pro-rated threshold of $13,650 is an ASSUMED input: the s 20 formula is not in the deposit.
-- Months of residency are months of the year of income: 1 is July, 4 is October, 6 is December.

